# D-Card API — events (host)
# Run top to bottom. Later requests reuse the event created here.


### Setup: provision the host
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Create an event (any signed-in user becomes its host)
# Required: planKey, eventTypeKey, title, startsAt (ISO with offset), contactName, contactPhone.
# Optional: endsAt, venueName, venueAddress, venueMapUrl, contact2Name, contact2Phone,
#   confirmationEnabled (default true), confirmationOffsetDays (0–30, default 2), headcountPct (0–100, default 70),
#   autoUpgradeEnabled (plan default; 422 if the plan does not allow it), singleAmount, doubleAmount,
#   budgetAmount (contribution target), reminderFrequencyDays (1–60), photoAlbumUrl.
# 201 → Event (same shape as GET /events/{id}, access "host") · 422 validation_error / invalid_phone.
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "planKey": "kawaida",
  "eventTypeKey": "wedding",
  "title": "Harusi ya Juma na Neema",
  "startsAt": "2026-12-12T15:00:00+03:00",
  "endsAt": "2026-12-12T22:00:00+03:00",
  "venueName": "Diamond Jubilee Hall",
  "venueAddress": "Upanga, Dar es Salaam",
  "venueMapUrl": "https://maps.google.com/?q=Diamond+Jubilee+Hall",
  "contactName": "Asha",
  "contactPhone": "0754 123 456",
  "singleAmount": 50000,
  "doubleAmount": 100000,
  "budgetAmount": 5000000
}

> {%
  client.global.set("eventId", response.body.id);
%}

### List my events (host or any team role)
# Newest first. `access` tells the caller's role: host|committee|treasurer|door_staff|walkin_approver.
# 200 → { "events": [Event…] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Get one event
# 200 → Event { id, title, status: draft|published|completed|cancelled, eventType, plan { key, name, pricePerGuest, guestLimit, paid },
#   startsAt, endsAt, timeZone, venue…, contact…, settings…, singleAmount, doubleAmount, budgetAmount, access, createdAt, updatedAt }
# 404 unknown/malformed id · 403 no role on this event.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}

### Someone without a role → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerToken}}

### Update event details and settings (host; draft or published only)
# Any subset of the create fields except planKey/eventTypeKey. Audited.
# 200 → Event · 409 event cancelled/completed · 422 validation.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "headcountPct": 75, "contact2Name": "Neema", "contact2Phone": "0713 222 333" }

### Validation error example → 422 with issues
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "headcountPct": 150, "venueMapUrl": "not a url" }

### Cancel the event (host) — run last; cancelled events are read-only
# 200 → Event with status "cancelled" · 409 already cancelled/completed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
